  "script": "The best NBA player from youngest to oldest, heading into next season. The youngest active NBA player is technically Cooper Flagg, but with that being said, the best 19-year-old in the NBA is Cooper Flagg. The best 20-year-old is Dylan Harper. The best 21-year-old is Stephon Castle. The best 22-year-old is Victor Wembanyama. The best 23-year-old, I'll take Paolo Banchero. But Amen Thompson is really close second. The best 24-year-old is Jalen Johnson, but Chet Holmgren also is a really close second. The best 25-year-old is Anthony Edwards, but Cade Cunningham is a really good second option, too. At 26, I'm taking Tyrese Haliburton, but if he doesn't come back 100%, my pick would go to Darius Garland. The best 27-year-old in the NBA is Luka Doncic. The best 28-year-old is Shai Gilgeous-Alexander. The best 29-year-old, it's either Devin Booker or Jalen Brown. The best 30-year-old is either Jalen Brunson or Donovan Mitchell. The best 31-year-old is a really tough call between Nikola Jokic and Giannis Antetokounmpo. The best 32-year-old is Joel Embiid. The best 33-year-old is Anthony Davis. The best 34-year-old is Kyrie Irving. The best 35-year-old is Kawhi Leonard. The best 36-year-old is Damian Lillard, but shout out to Draymond Green. The best 37-year-old is, technically, James Harden. I know Kevin Durant is 37 as of this recording, but he will be 38 before the season starts. With that being said, the best 38-year-old is Steph Curry. The best 39-year-old is Mike Conley. The best 40-year-old is Al Horford. And the best 41-year-old, the oldest player in the NBA, is LeBron James.",
